# Census Geocoder
# Geocodes coordinates via the US Census Bureau geocoding API.
#
# Input: latitude, longitude
# Output: record with status, tract_geoid, county_name, county_fips, state_name, state_fips
#
# Usage:
#   devlish run lib/census_geocoder.dvl --input '{"latitude": 32.7767, "longitude": -96.7970}'

inputs:
  latitude
  longitude

census url equals "https://geocoding.geo.census.gov/geocoder/geographies/coordinates?x=" plus longitude plus "&y=" plus latitude plus "&benchmark=Public_AR_Current&vintage=Census2020_Current&format=json"

Get the url at census url as api response

response body equals body of api response
api result equals result of response body
geo equals geographies of api result

If geo is missing:
  Fail with record with "no_geographies" as status and latitude as latitude and longitude as longitude

Respond with record with "matched" as status and latitude as latitude and longitude as longitude and geo as geographies
